quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  2,62,"Indeed, the (Muslim) believers, the Jews, the Christians and the Sabians—all those who (sincerely) believe in Allah and the Last Day and act piously shall have their reward with their Lord. There shall be no fear on them, nor shall they grieve."
  2,63,"(Remember) when We took a pledge from you and raised the Mount (of Sinai) above you, (and said:) ‘Hold fast to what We have given you, and bear its contents in mind, so that you may be God-conscious.’"
  2,64,"Even after that, you turned away. Had it not been for Allah’s favour and His mercy on you, you would have certainly been among the losers."
  2,65,"Certainly, you know those of you who violated the Sabbath. So We said to them: ‘Be like apes: disgraced and rejected.’"
  2,66,"So, We made it an exemplary punishment for the present and for succeeding generations, and a lesson to those who are God-conscious."
  2,67,"(Recall) when Musa (Moses) said to his people: ‘Indeed, Allah commands you to slaughter a cow.’ They said: ‘Are you making fun of us?’ Musa (Moses) said: ‘I seek Allah’s protection from being among the ignorant.’"
  2,68,"They said: ‘Call upon your Lord for us, that He may clarify for us what she is.’ He answered: ‘God says the cow should neither be too old nor too young, but in between. So do as you are commanded.’"
  2,69,"They said: ‘Call upon your Lord for us, that He may clarify for us what her colour should be.’ He said: ‘God says it should be yellow, a bright yellow cow, pleasing to the viewers.’"
